 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Not exactly. It's more than that because you need to cover distance without getting too tired. A good target is 20 miles or 6 hours, whichever comes first. Roughly four hours, so plan for a full working day with somewhere to stop and get off your horse. It is, and you need time for stops as well. A typical horse can only go so far every hour, so you need shorter daylight hours. Start with shorter ones to build up your skills and fitness. Ten miles is nice length for a weekend day ride. Start with shorter outings on trails you already know, and gradually increase. A good rule of thumb is double the distance you've ridden before and cut it back by half if you feel overwhelmed.",
